<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 6-mth T-bill av yield falls to 14.80 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 6-mth T-bill av yield falls to 14.80 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of six-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to an annual 14.80 percent at an auction from 15.05 percent at the last auction on June 23, the National Bank said on Tuesday. Details of the auction--</p>
<p>					   July 7	     June 23</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ46K0801980     KZ46K2512973</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  600		  600</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 1,974		1,735</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 606		  607</p>
<p> Average price			 93.11 pct	  93.00</p>
<p> Average yield			 14.80 pct	  15.05</p>
<p> Tenor				   182 days	   182 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Jan 8, 1998	Dec 25, 1998</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
